    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #330\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nNo uncommitted changes remained; pushed the new commit to the existing branch `bb/relay-231-mcp-integration-03-07-add-an-mcp-clien-thr_7zw42dhena` (already tracking origin from earlier in this conversation).\n\n## Summary\n\nPushed commit `aa217af` (\"Address code review on #330\") to `bb/relay-231-mcp-integration-03-07-add-an-mcp-clien-thr_7zw42dhena`, which addresses all 3 findings from the PR #330 code review:\n\n1. Bounded `mcpClient.connect(transport)` with a 15s default timeout (overridable) so a server that never answers `initialize` can't hang the factory indefinitely.\n2. `resolveCredential` no longer misreports transient DB failures as `credential_decryption_failed` — only genuine decrypt/master-key errors get that classification.\n3. Fixed the stdio contract test server's `getHandshakeCount()` to return a real accumulating count instead of a boolean cast to 0/1.\n\nFull test suite (unit: 83 tests, integration: 539 tests, e2e: 5 tests), the dependency-boundary check, and the full monorepo build all pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
