    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #330\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed to branch `bb/relay-231-mcp-integration-03-07-add-an-mcp-clien-thr_7zw42dhena`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis push addresses the round-3 code review finding on PR #330 (CI run `101919493397`):\n\n**Medium correctness finding**: `buildStdioTransport` in `backend/packages/data/src/mcp/mcpConnectionFactory.ts` stripped `StdioClientTransport`'s default environment (`PATH`, `HOME`, etc.) whenever a credential was injected without an explicit `config.env`. The SDK only falls back to `getDefaultEnvironment()`'s safe allowlist when `env` is entirely `undefined` — any other defined object becomes the complete child environment with no merge. Since the credential-injection path always produced a defined object (`{ [credentialEnvVar]: credential }`), any stdio MCP server relying on ambient environment variables would break in that configuration.\n\n**Fix** (commit `c610e8e`): import `getDefaultEnvironment` from the SDK's stdio module, and whenever a defined `env` object is needed at all (`config.env` present and/or credential injection), seed it from `getDefaultEnvironment()` first, then layer `config.env` and the injected credential on top — matching the reviewer's suggested fix.\n\nVerified in this turn:\n- `tsc --noEmit` — clean\n- Unit tests — 83/83 passed\n- Integration tests (includes `mcpConnectionFactory.test.ts`) — 539/539 passed\n- E2E tests — 5/5 passed\n- Dependency-boundary check — no violations\n\nAll three rounds of review findings on this PR are now resolved.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
